{"id": "EUVD-2026-57040", "enisaUuid": "ad535015-5c6f-3193-b4d2-26b93fbce661", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink\n\nA tunnel changelink() operates on at most two netns, dev_net(dev) and\nthe sticky underlay netns vxlan->net. They differ once the device is\ncreated in or moved to a netns other than the one the request runs in.\nThe rtnl changelink path checks CAP_NET_ADMIN only against dev_net(dev),\nso a caller privileged there but not in vxlan->net can rewrite a vxlan\ndevice whose underlay lives in vxlan->net.\n\nvxlan_changelink() validates and applies the new configuration against\nvxlan->net (vxlan_config_validate(vxlan->net, ...)) and can reopen the\nunderlay socket in that netns, so the same reasoning as the tunnel\nchangelink series applies here.\n\nGate vxlan_changelink() with rtnl_dev_link_net_capable(), at the top of\nthe op before any attribute is parsed, matching ipgre_changelink() and\nthe rest of the \"require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for\nchangelink\" series.\n\nFound by 0sec automated security-research tooling (https://0sec.ai).", "datePublished": "2026-08-12T00:07:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:09:10", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b95a8743e58f7efed5ddc4cb73829b66f17feab0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7465ade989ba84adc2bfa58bad3ca25d249f0f7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0aa580a8bbbed2507b4582a1f0ef581d480d06ed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b3793d7dccb192ffff29894d11824db6251acdd5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32d10c46bfde3e9b274e9e1bd6399d0ebea8f60f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/730c7e5fea7f06e0cdf21c547222ec93234fd1d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8ad0d311e225939a9a6c745d6cc384c7364ec87", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a61bd9637f3d929aa846e4eb3d98b48c26fcb0e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mq37-5gx6-p5gp", "CVE-2026-68432"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "38829df4-deb7-3c91-b017-827689e75a3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bcdc4f3a20be949df54b67e5ae2734daabb5792 <3a61bd9637f3d929aa846e4eb3d98b48c26fcb0e"}, {"id": "4184b1c9-0072-3e4f-bc36-3cdcabd41703", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "504d5774-0857-3e64-8cbc-79675f9c1ba4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "5378f2da-c193-304a-8216-0a623f35a7ca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bcdc4f3a20be949df54b67e5ae2734daabb5792 <b95a8743e58f7efed5ddc4cb73829b66f17feab0"}, {"id": "63dc317f-4fb8-306e-8ea9-561e0741094b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6d99d797-cb15-3fd6-89f4-e75c0683cb2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.11"}, {"id": "740737fe-9249-37dc-bd52-c2f215d3b339", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bcdc4f3a20be949df54b67e5ae2734daabb5792 <0aa580a8bbbed2507b4582a1f0ef581d480d06ed"}, {"id": "7dfc54d3-aa0c-3850-89ca-15f13b5db3be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "967a707d-cf5c-34e4-90ca-83eddcfd399a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bcdc4f3a20be949df54b67e5ae2734daabb5792 <b3793d7dccb192ffff29894d11824db6251acdd5"}, {"id": "a21ea190-cbb5-3f56-ab7e-048883f84c7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "a4b4616c-1c5e-3a38-b04c-3f7d5e75489a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bcdc4f3a20be949df54b67e5ae2734daabb5792 <32d10c46bfde3e9b274e9e